# The HTTP activity panel (src/app/http_panel.zig, painter
# src/ui/http_panel.zig): seven collapsible sections in the left column,
# COLLECTIONS a folder tree, one `/` filter across them all, an empty
# section's words and its `+ New …` link, the three action links last.
# Entering opens a blank request pane in the centre and gives it the
# keys (Rust's `entering_http`); a click on the filter pill takes them.
write api/users.http "GET https://x/users\n"
write api/orders.curl "curl https://x/orders\n"
write api/orders.curl.mock.json "{\"status\":200,\"body\":\"[]\"}\n"
write .mnml/env/dev.env "HOST=https://dev\n"
write .mnml/env/prod.env "HOST=https://prod\n"
write .mnml/chains/login.chain.json "[{\"request\":\"api/users.http\"}]\n"
write .mnml/cookies.json "{\"x.test\":{\"session\":\"abc\"}}\n"
write .rqst/history.jsonl "{\"ts\":1,\"method\":\"POST\",\"url\":\"https://x/login\",\"status\":201}\n"
command view.activity_http
expect screen contains "HTTP (8)"
expect screen contains "GET  new request"
expect pane GET
expect screen contains "COLLECTIONS (2)"
expect screen contains "api (2)"
expect screen contains "users.http"
expect screen contains "ENVS (2)"
expect screen contains "● dev"
expect screen contains "○ prod"
expect screen contains "+ New env"
expect screen contains "CHAINS (1)"
expect screen contains "+ New chain"
expect screen contains "MOCKS (1)"
expect screen contains "api/orders.curl"
expect screen contains "COOKIES (1)"
expect screen contains "session  x.test"
expect screen contains "RECENT (1)"
expect screen contains "201 POST x/login"
expect screen contains "CAPTURED (0)"
expect screen contains "Nothing captured yet"
# The filter pill takes the keys; typing narrows every section at
# once; the ones it empties go, and so do the words and links.
click 10 2
type log
expect screen contains "(2 of 8)"
expect screen contains "CHAINS (1)"
expect screen contains "RECENT (1)"
expect screen lacks "ENVS"
expect screen lacks "COOKIES"
expect screen lacks "+ New chain"
key esc
key esc
expect screen contains "ENVS (2)"
# Enter on the COLLECTIONS header folds it; right opens it again.
key enter
expect screen lacks "users.http"
expect screen contains "COLLECTIONS (2)"
key right
expect screen contains "users.http"
# Down walks the folder, its two files, skips the gap, the ENVS
# header, dev, prod: enter makes prod the session override.
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "env: prod (session override"
expect screen contains "● prod"
# Row 3 is users.http: enter opens it as a request pane.
key g
key down
key down
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "https://x/users"
expect pane GET
